# Auth Server

This component is solely responsible for decorating and integration with the hydra and kratos
identity components to enrich the token with various bits of information.

It is expected that kratos is configured to point at this address to webhook post the login and token hook
inputs. You can find these in kratos configuration.

```
ory:
  kratos:
    // ...
    selfservice:
      // ...
      flows:
        login:
          web_hook: "http://local.dev.klustr.io:7878/ory/kratos/login?apikey=XXXX"
```

For token enrichment this comes from the hydra side of configuraiton

```
ory:
  hydra:
    // ...
    oauth2:
      token_hook: "http://local.dev.klustr.io:7878/ory/hydra/token_hook"
      expose_internal_errors: "false"
```

In the future this webhook should have some type of credential exchange (api key) so that
the webhook can validate who is calling it or use mtls or something similar to authorize
the request.

By default the apis are accessible once the server starts here;
- http://localhost:7878/swagger-ui/index.html

Health metrics area here
- http://localhost:7878/actuator/metrics
- http://localhost:7878/actuator/health